        {
          "id": "p19-q28-stem",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "align": "left",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Four Year 12 students want to organise a graduation party."
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "All four students have the same probability, "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "P(F)",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", of being available next Friday."
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "All four students have the same probability, "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "P(S)",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", of being available next Saturday."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p19-q28-givens",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "align": "left",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "It is given that "
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "P(F)=\\frac{3}{10},\\quad P(S\\mid F)=\\frac{1}{3},\\quad\\text{and}\\quad P(F\\mid S)=\\frac{1}{8}.",
              "display": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p19-q28-kim",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "align": "left",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Kim is one of the four students."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q28-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Is Kim's availability next Friday independent from his availability next Saturday? Justify your answer.",
        "answerSpaceMm": 22,
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not independent, since $P(F\\mid S)=\\frac18\\ne\\frac{3}{10}=P(F)$.",
          "worked": "For independence, $P(F)=P(F\\mid S)$. Here,\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(F)&=\\frac{3}{10},\\\\P(F\\mid S)&=\\frac18.\\end{aligned}$$\nSince $\\frac{3}{10}\\ne\\frac18$, Kim's availability on the two days is not independent."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q28-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that the probability that Kim is available next Saturday is $\\frac45$.",
        "answerSpaceMm": 67,
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(S)=\\frac45$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}P(S\\mid F)&=\\frac{P(S\\cap F)}{P(F)},\\\\\\frac13&=\\frac{P(S\\cap F)}{\\frac{3}{10}},\\\\P(S\\cap F)&=\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(F\\mid S)&=\\frac{P(S\\cap F)}{P(S)},\\\\\\frac18&=\\frac{\\frac{1}{10}}{P(S)},\\\\P(S)&=\\frac{1}{10}\\times8\\\\P(S)&=\\frac45.\\end{aligned}$$"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q28-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Assume that the four students' availabilities next Saturday are independent of one another. What is the probability that at least one of the four students is NOT available next Saturday?",
        "answerSpaceMm": 36,
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{369}{625}$.",
          "worked": "Using independence between students,\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(\\text{all four available})&=\\left(\\frac45\\right)^4\\\\P(\\text{all four available})&=\\frac{256}{625}.\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(\\text{at least one not available})&=1-P(\\text{all four available})\\\\P(\\text{at least one not available})&=1-\\frac{256}{625}\\\\P(\\text{at least one not available})&=\\frac{369}{625}.\\end{aligned}$$"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
